* A basic CHARMM script
* Nov 2011, Universitaet Wien, Stefan Boresch
* |
* Default nonbonded options are used. Should you use this file as
* the basis for real work, please check whether these settings are appropriate
*

! Many CHARMM scripts follow the same basic pattern 
!     (which you'll see over and over again)
! (A) Read generic files for class of molecules studied (RTF/PRM)
!        here we read a so-called 'stream' file which does all the work
! (B) Read specifics of system (PSF/CRD)
!    --- now we are ready to do something ---
! (C) Set various parameters/options (e.g., nonbonded cutoff radius, 
!     use of periodic boundary conditions, use of SHAKE
! (D) Calculate energy, minimize, run MC or MD
! (E) Optional: Do some (quick and dirty) analysis what happened in (D)
! (F) Save new coordinates (plus other information should it have changed)
!

! Read RTF and parameter files (A)

stream toppar.str ! does all the work

! Read PSF and coordinate file (B)

read psf card name psf_coor/1crn.psf

read coor card name psf_coor/1crn_init.crd

! Step (C) omitted 

! Calculate the energy (D) 

energy ! here you could finetune the energy options

! Minimize: 100 steps steepest descent (SD), 100 steps adopted basis set 
!      Newton Raphson (ABNR)

mini sd nstep 100
mini abnr nstep 100

! Step (E) omitted.

! Save new coordinates in pdb and crd format (F)

writ coor card name psf_coor/1crn_somemini.crd
* CRAMBIN, from pdb entry 1crn,
* with CHARMM27 parameter set
* after 100 steps SD + 100 steps ABNR minimization
*

! write coordinates also in pdb format
! important to (re)import structures into externan (graphics) programs 
! that don't understand CHARMM format
writ coor pdb name psf_coor/1crn_somemini.pdb
* CRAMBIN, from pdb entry 1crn,
* with CHARMM27 parameter set
* after 100 steps SD + 100 steps ABNR minimization
*

stop